<!--
Lite-mode managed-stripping protection.

Background: in Unity 2022.3 IL2CPP builds (especially Release with managed
stripping = High), the linker walks the IL reference graph and drops any
type that does not appear reachable. The Lite-mode REPL is at risk in three
distinct ways:

  1. System.Linq.Expressions.Interpreter — internal to the BCL and only
     activated at runtime via LambdaExpression.Compile(preferInterpretation:
     true). Static analysis sees Compile() but does not necessarily reach
     every Interpreter instruction subclass. If even one instruction class is
     stripped, the interpreter falls back to LightCompiler then fails on AOT
     with "Operation is not supported on this platform."

  2. The codec primitives (BinaryReader / BinaryWriter / MemoryStream /
     UTF8Encoding) are directly referenced from LiteWireReader/Writer so
     they should survive. Preserving them explicitly is a belt-and-suspenders
     guard against unusual linker decisions on the Player.

  3. The reflection types resolved at runtime via Type.GetType(AQN) are
     USER types. Those must be preserved by the user's own link.xml or
     [UnityEngine.Scripting.Preserve] / [JsonSerializable] usage — this
     file does not (and cannot) enumerate them.

Reference: Docs~/ExpressionInterpreterFeasibility_zh.md §3.1 task 7,
§7.4 IL2CPP stripping. Task 7 also requires an actual IL2CPP build run
against spike-equivalent cases (deferred to hands-on player testing).
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="System.Linq.Expressions" preserve="all" />
  <assembly fullname="System.Core" preserve="all" />
  <assembly fullname="mscorlib">
    <type fullname="System.IO.BinaryReader" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="System.IO.BinaryWriter" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="System.IO.MemoryStream" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="System.Text.UTF8Encoding" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="System.Text.Encoding" preserve="all" />
  </assembly>
  <assembly fullname="netstandard">
    <type fullname="System.IO.BinaryReader" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="System.IO.BinaryWriter" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="System.IO.MemoryStream" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="System.Text.UTF8Encoding" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="System.Text.Encoding" preserve="all" />
  </assembly>
</linker>
